@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Playtest 2 — newest sessions
+
+**Verdict: FAIL — three major findings; no blocker found.** Tested the existing production site at `http://localhost:3417` on 2026-11-01. No server lifecycle/build commands or `src/` edits.
+
+## Findings
+
+1. **Major · bug · Café c4-1–6: nine pictures do not load.** Both devices show blank scenes for `rounds/c4-4.webp` through `c4-6.webp`, and blank results for **all six** `after/c4-*.webp` images. Direct asset URLs and Next image requests return 404 even though the files exist locally. Evidence: [phone c4-4](../qa/playtest-2/phone/c4-4-start.png), [desktop c4-1 result](../qa/playtest-2/desktop/cafe-c4-1-correct.png), [HTTP results](../qa/playtest-2/asset-check.json); image selection at `src/games/cafe/CafeGame.tsx:133`. **Fix:** include all twelve assets in the production artifact before the next authorized build/deployment; verify every direct and optimized URL returns an image. The observed failure is serving, not absence from this checkout.
+
+2. **Major · defensible answers rejected · Family f3-3/f3-4.** English → Morse code → “can be written down” produces “It isn't true…” and counts a miss. “Can tell a story” is also rejected. Morse encodes written messages; its own card depicts a paper record. The newcomer also claims the builders' language “cannot be written down,” confusing an unwritten practice with impossibility. Evidence: [writing rejection](../qa/playtest-2/phone/f3-3-morse-writing-rejected.png), [story rejection](../qa/playtest-2/phone/f3-3-morse-story-rejected.png), [builders rejection](../qa/playtest-2/phone/f3-4-wrong.png); `src/games/family/rounds.ts:91,175`, `FamilyGame.tsx:319,336`. **Fix:** accept Morse writing/story links; either describe the builders as “not written in this example” or allow the literal capability. Audit the remaining “can” labels against their feature flags. [ITU Morse specification](https://www.itu.int/dms_pubrec/itu-r/rec/m/R-REC-M.1677-1-200910-I%21%21PDF-E.pdf).
+
+3. **Major · misleading English rule · Go On! p-5.** The successful explanation says future verbs take *to* and most others take *-ing*. A B1 learner can transfer that rule to “consider to leave tomorrow” or “avoid to swim tomorrow.” Both require *-ing*, despite future reference. Evidence: `src/games/pupil/levels.ts:161,181`; [explanation](../qa/playtest-2/phone/p-5-start.png). **Fix:** teach explicit verb groups, or label this a limited guess and demonstrate its failure before completion. “After enjoy, finish, mind and avoid, use -ing; after want, hope, decide and plan, use to + verb” fits this exercise. [British Council grammar](https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar/a1-a2/verbs-followed-ing-or-infinitive).
+
+4. **Minor · misleading counter · Go On! p-5/p-6.** Clicking an explanation increments “Cards used,” although no example card was shown. In p-5, one example plus two explanations becomes “All five right with 3 cards.” Evidence: [explanation counted](../qa/playtest-2/phone/p-5-bad-explanation.png), [result](../qa/playtest-2/phone/p-5-trained.png); `src/games/pupil/PupilGame.tsx:65–70,162,180,189`. **Fix:** count example cards separately; if explanations should cost a move, label the total “Teaching steps” and compare it with a minimum calculated on the same basis.
+
+5. **Minor · arguable wrong option · Café c4-3.** “Bye! Have a nice day!” is rejected because Rosa has just entered. A person leaving the café can hold the door for someone entering, wish them a nice day, and continue holding it. Neither the clues nor this option excludes that ordinary situation. Evidence: `src/games/cafe/rounds.ts:363–370`; [scene and choices](../qa/playtest-2/phone/c4-3-start.png). **Fix:** establish that you and Rosa are arriving together, or make the option explicitly abandon the door before she is through. This is an authored-option ambiguity; that specific rejection was not clicked.
+
+6. **Minor · citation overreach · Family / PI §18.** The gloss names chemistry and **music notation** as the new suburbs, “built for one job.” §18 names chemistry and **calculus notation**; music and the single-job gloss are the game's extension. Evidence: `src/content/sources.ts:96`; [primary text, §18](https://www.wittgensteinproject.org/w/index.php/Philosophische_Untersuchungen). **Fix:** “Wittgenstein compares chemistry and calculus notation to new suburbs. This game extends that comparison to music notation.” Keep the quotation separate from the analogy.
+
+7. **Minor · conflicting instructions/art · Family session 3.** About still says “Six cards show things we call games,” while these cards are languages/sign systems. Completion also shows the games cover. Evidence: `src/content/games.ts:86`; [phone completion](../qa/playtest-2/phone/family-end.png), [desktop completion](../qa/playtest-2/desktop/family-recovery-done.png). **Fix:** make instructions and cover depend on the selected session. Local `FamilyGame.tsx` already contains session-specific artwork changes; verify the next production artifact actually includes them instead of reimplementing that change.
+
+8. **Minor · picture weakens vocabulary clue · Slab b4-5.** The two “slabs” resemble masonry platforms assembled from several blocks. That blurs the slab/block distinction precisely when the learner must identify one slab. Evidence: [phone picture](../qa/playtest-2/phone/b4-5-start.png), `public/art/builder/use/b4-5.webp`. **Fix:** show two single, continuous stone slabs of different sizes, without internal masonry joints.
+
+## Coverage and limits
+
+Python Playwright, headless Chromium; phone **390×844 with touch**, desktop **1280×860**. Selected the requested sessions through **Sessions** and completed all 18 rounds on each device: b4-1–6, c4-1–6, f3-1–4, p-5/p-6. Tried wrong choices throughout, clarification questions, partial threads and pupil explanations. Eight phone reload comparisons and fourteen desktop comparisons preserved the recorded text/state. No JavaScript page errors or horizontal page overflow observed. Screenshots were visually inspected; all twelve Café source pictures were also inspected separately from their production availability.
+
+Evidence: [phone actions/text/image checks](../qa/playtest-2/phone/actions.json), [phone errors](../qa/playtest-2/phone/errors.json), [desktop coverage and commands](../qa/playtest-2/desktop/summary.json). Phone runs: `python qa/playtest-2/phone_play.py` and the same command with `cafe`, `family`, or `pupil`. Earlier selector/resume mistakes were test-script failures, recovered before completion; they are not app findings.
+
+**Not covered:** physical phones, Safari/Firefox, audible speech, keyboard-only/accessibility behavior, every possible answer path, or the Family “unlike” route. Philosophy review checked section meaning/attribution against the primary German text, not every word of the English translation. Missing production pictures prevented checking their responsive rendering. B1 judgments are editorial, not learner-study results.
+
+**Also done:** captured failed asset requests and a source-file hash baseline to distinguish serving failures from content changes. Undo: remove this task's `qa/playtest-2/` evidence and `planning/playtest-codex-2.md`. Existing work was left intact.
